05:18.250 --> 05:22.170
<b>On Academy Island, aside from District 0, 
each district has one academy in it,</b>

05:22.170 --> 05:24.350
<b>meaning there are 20 academies in total.</b>

05:24.750 --> 05:27.890
<b>These academies get ranked 
and scored every year.</b>

05:27.090 --> 05:27.890
<b><i>Ouka Academy</i></b>

05:27.090 --> 05:27.890
<b><i>Tenonzaka Academy</i></b>

05:27.090 --> 05:27.890
<b><i>Shinra High School</i></b>

05:27.090 --> 05:27.890
<b><i>Suisei Academy</i></b>

05:27.090 --> 05:27.890
<b><i>Eimei Academy</i></b>

05:28.460 --> 05:32.880
<b>The academies are given a number 
of benefits based on their ranking.</b>

05:33.280 --> 05:36.690
<b>Huh. Do the students' Stars 
have anything to do with it?</b>

05:36.690 --> 05:38.010
<b>Indeed they do.</b>

05:38.010 --> 05:41.840
<b>Students with five or more Stars are 
generally considered to be advanced.</b>

05:41.840 --> 05:44.990
<b>The more advanced students an 
academy has, the higher it ranks,</b>

05:44.990 --> 05:48.400
<b>and if it has a Seven Star student, 
it will almost certainly end up top.</b>

05:48.800 --> 05:52.230
<b>No wonder the headmistress
is super on board with that.</b>

05:52.230 --> 05:56.900
<b>And that is exactly why the Seven Stars 
get targeted by everyone on the island.</b>

05:57.190 --> 06:02.110
<b>I can see why. If a Six Star beats me,
 they take my place at the top.</b>

06:02.110 --> 06:05.100
<b>Even so, don't we bet 
our own Stars in games?</b>

06:05.100 --> 06:05.930
<b>Yes.</b>

06:05.930 --> 06:10.340
<b>However, the returns are very large, so if
there is even a small chance of winning,</b>

06:10.340 --> 06:12.820
<b>it may be worth knowingly taking the risk.</b>

06:12.820 --> 06:15.440
